Please note that the `Debug.Assert()` statements will only generate and run correctly when the application is built with debugging information. These statements do not provide any meaningful output when a condition fails, they are more suited for debugging and testing purposes. Additionally, these assertions won't halt the program or throw an exception when a condition is not met, this is a feature of .NET itself - your program will continue running as normal.
